    kgjobs:firstSeenAt "2026-09-03T07:45:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:lastSeenAt "2026-09-03T07:45:01+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    kgjobs:reconciliationReason "no reviewed first-party candidate" ;
    kgjobs:sourceOccurrence <https://openknowledgegraphs.com/jobs/live/occurrence/arbeitnow-associate-privacy-consultant-smb-munich-192881/1> ;
    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "associate-privacy-consultant-smb-munich-192881" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "YOUR JOB Do you want to work on privacy topics where your expertise has visible customer impact, not just theoretical relevance? As an Associate Privacy Consultant, you take ownership of an established customer base and help companies turn GDPR requirements into clear, pragmatic and scalable privacy practices. You will work at the intersection of privacy, SaaS and AI enabled consulting, advising customers hands-on while shaping how modern privacy consulting can become smarter, faster and more impactful. If you bring strong data protection knowledge, customer instinct and the drive to raise the bar in a high ownership environment, then join us on our journey. WE PROTECT THE PEOPLE BEHIND THE DATA We are a fast-growing security and compliance tech company with a clear purpose: we protect the people behind the data. With over 200 team members worldwide and with offices in Munich, Berlin, London, Stockholm, and Vienna, we help more than 4,000 global customers get certified fast and build a strong and scalable risk posture. With AI-powered automation, self-serve capabilities, and additional tailored expert advice, we offer our customers a seamless security and compliance experience to stay ahead of the rapidly evolving security landscape and challenges like the surge in cyber-attacks. WHAT YOU'LL BE DOING You advise and support your own customer base on data protection, combining privacy expertise with smart use of our AI-powered platform., having a strong focus on retention, customer health and long-term value creation. You translate complex GDPR and privacy topics into clear, pragmatic guidance that helps customers make confident business decisions. You help customers use DataGuard as their central privacy hub and actively drive platform adoption, engagement and monthly active usage. You use AI tools thoughtfully in privacy related workflows and critically review AI generated outputs based on your subject matter expertise. You collaborate with privacy, automation and product stakeholders to share customer insights and contribute to more scalable, tech enabled consulting workflows. WHAT YOU'LL GET IN RETURN Real ownership of an established customer base from day one A steep learning curve through hands-on advisory work with diverse privacy customers The chance to work at the intersection of privacy, SaaS and AI enabled consulting High visibility in a business critical, customer-facing role with direct impact on retention, adoption and expansion Close collaboration with experienced privacy consultants, automation experts and product stakeholders Structured onboarding, continuous learning opportunities and support for relevant certifications A training budget of 1,500, access to personal coaching and support for certifications such as TÜV Datenschutzbeauftragter, CIPP/E or AIGP A collaborative, international team that values curiosity, ownership and pragmatic problem solving THE QUALITIES YOU'LL NEED FOR A SUCCESSFUL CAREER AT DATAGUARD 2+ years of relevant experience in privacy consulting, customer advisory, audits or handling privacy related customer requests. Strong GDPR and privacy knowledge, ideally combined with a legal, business law or comparable privacy focused background. Ability to turn complex privacy requirements into simple, structured and customer-friendly recommendations. Ability to improve efficiency in a dynamic customer environment, spot opportunities to create more value, and stay focused even when priorities shift. Entrepreneurial mindset, ownership and the ability to connect the dots between customer needs, platform usage and business impact. Curiosity to AI tools and automation, paired with the judgment to review AI generated privacy content critically. Native level fluency in German, strong professional English skills LAST BUT NOT LEAST. FROM THE BOTTOM OF OUR HEARTS: No matter your origin, ethnicity, gender identity, religion or individual requirements; at DataGuard, all that counts is the person you are. As Guards and Guardettes, we are united not only by our dedication, but also by our shared belief in our purpose: Protect the people behind the data. Convince us with your personality and your skills – and together we will make great things happen. We are looking forward to meeting you! #LI-DNI Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
