    schema:description "About Munich Electrification Munich Electrification is an innovative company founded with the aim of accelerating the transition to electric and connected mobility. We develop innovative electronic control units for electric vehicles and stationary storage systems for our global customers. Our international team is composed of highly motivated and exceptional engineers. As a small and specialized team we are well-aware of the importance of each individual colleague and support and promote each employee according to their abilities and needs. Our office with adjacent prototype and testing lab is located in the heart of Munich at the Heimeranplatz. This is what we stand for: - Technological Leadership: We challenge norms, innovate quickly, and anticipate future needs. We take smart risks and learn from outcomes to stay ahead. - Sustainability: We actively drive change for a sustainable future, aware of our impact and inspiring others to build a better world. - Team Culture: We believe work should be enjoyable, fostering a spirit of inspiration, celebration, and teamwork across the globe. - Entrepreneurial Spirit: We embrace change, think big, and push limits with passion. Your Role: Your primary mission is to own and evolve our Digital Ecosystem, ensuring our cloud-first infrastructure is as innovative and high-performing as our battery technology. You will ensure that our core platforms (Google Workspace and the Atlassian) function as a seamless, interconnected network that empowers our company. Acting as the vital bridge between business requirements and technical execution, you will master the configuration of existing solutions and be the technical lead for new application/service implementations. Key Responsibilities: SaaS & Cloud Governance: Act as the Platform Owner for Google Workspace and Atlassian, managing configurations, security, and permissions. Business Process Evolution: Work with department heads to translate business needs into scalable digital workflows. Vendor & Stakeholder Contact: Coordinate with external consultants and developers. Documentation & Training: Maintain high-quality documentation of our application landscape and lead training sessions for power users. Your Profile: Education: Degree in Business Informatics, Computer Science, or equivalent professional experience. Experience: Min. 3-5 years of experience as a Full-time Cloud/IT Administrator. Proven track record in Application Management, specifically with MDM systems and Cloud/SaaS environments. Technical Expertise: Good knowledge of Atlassian and Google Workspace administration. Analytical Mindset: You enjoy mapping complex business processes into clean, digital solutions. Communication: Fluent in English; German is a plus; Ability to explain technical concepts to non-IT stakeholders. Optional: Experience with AWS. Experience with Google Cloud Identity & SSO integrations. Certification in ITIL SAP Knowledge: Practical experience with SAP (ByDesign or S/4HANA). Our Offer & Benefits The chance to be part of a highly innovative, agile, and unique team with prestigious customers in the automotive and battery storage sector. You will gain a deeper knowledge around connected & electric vehicle batteries, battery management and electronics development and strive in an exciting work environment Benefits (Full-time Employees): - Trust-based working hours and hybrid work - Adequate and competitive compensation - Pension Plan/Bonus - Free access to the fitness center right next to us or subsidized EGYM Wellpass - Free snacks, coffee, drinks and lunch (freshly cooked by our chef) every day - Public transport ticket - Bike-Leasing via Business Bike - Experience various inspiring and fun team events - ME-branded clothing - Option to \"work from anywhere\" (6 weeks/year) Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Full Time" ;
    schema:hiringOrganization kgjd:employer-munich-electrification ;
