    schema:datePosted "2026-09-02"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "We are Isarsoft We make every camera count At ​Isarsoft ​we develop video analytics software ​to make transportation and cities more efficient, inclusive and secure. ​We stand for data protection and responsible processing of sensitive data. Being ​on the forefront of innovation we work together in interdisciplinary teams in a positive, fun and energetic atmosphere. Our customers and partners are at the center of everything we do. ​Founded in 2019 ​​we have ​grown organically winning large customers ​and partners delivering compelling, reliable, high-performance software. We are proud of being a privately held company with family atmosphere focusing on long-term relations to our customers and team members. Your mission Support Customer Success: Assist in engaging with customers to understand their technical needs and use cases for Isarsoft Perception. Bridge Tech & Requirements: Work alongside our engineering team to help translate customer feedback into actionable product requirements. Hands-on Technical Support: Partner with sales and engineering teams during technical workshops, product demos, and onboarding. Product Improvement: Help investigate new feature opportunities based on real user data and customer feedback. Your profile Enrolled student in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Science, or a related technical field (ideally with at least 2 semesters remaining). First practical experience (through projects, internships, or courses) in SQL, Python, and working with APIs/SDKs. Strong communication skills and a problem-solving mindset with a focus on helping users. Fluency in both English and German (min. C1 level required). Ability to work up to 20 hours/week during the semester (flexible during semester breaks). Additional assets Familiarity with Docker or Linux environments. Basic understanding of Computer Vision or AI applications. Prior experience in a startup or fast-paced tech environment Modern development workflow proficiency, including the confident and reliable use of AI coding assistants (e.g., Claude Code, Cursor). Strong foundation in version control systems (Git) and hands-on experience with CI/CD pipelines Benefits An experienced, highly motivated and international team to learn and grow A high-impact work environment with flat hierarchies and short decision-making processes Have the flexibility to work from anywhere: A great office in Munich, from home or the English-Garden Free lunch, coffee and drinks at our office Sounds good? We are just getting started. Let's build a great company together. Hiring Process We are committed to a transparent and fair hiring process. We aim for concluding the interview process in no longer than 2 weeks. The following three stages are typical for any position at Isarsoft. Video Interview with HR Technical Deep Dive We deeply believe that a great product only can be build by a great team. That's why sharing our values, being a team-player and having a energetic attitude is as important as bringing the right technical skills. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
