    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "working-student-catena-x-project-management-implementation-reutlingen-152810" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-09-03"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "Join us in driving connectivity forward! At One Mobility Group, we bridge worlds—combining nearly a century of German automotive engineering precision with the innovation power of the globe's largest electronics and ICT manufacturer. This unique positioning makes us the strategic partner for end-to-end mobility solutions—from initial concept design to large-scale manufacturing. Our comprehensive portfolio spans the full spectrum of electrified mobility, including power distribution systems, high- and low-voltage modules, safety components, and advanced charging solutions. We specialize in integration expertise that seamlessly connects data, power, and sensing – redefining what’s possible in intelligent, connected mobility. At One Mobility, you will join a vibrant international team of 10,500 people, working together in 17 countries across Europe, Asia, North America, the Middle East, and Africa. Step into a culture where inclusivity is the foundation, where your ideas are trusted and supported, your passions are nurtured, and the spirit of collaboration is encouraged. We move fast, think differently, and empower our people to deliver breakthrough solutions. We are looking for Working Student (m/f/d) Catena-X Project Management & Implementation Duration: 4–6 months Your tasks: The working student supports the successful introduction and further development of Catena-X within the company and takes on project responsibilities independently, including the management of defined sub-projects. Support and independently contribute to the implementation of Catena-X requirements and solutions within the company Coordinate and track project activities with internal and external stakeholders Take ownership of sub-projects and, in the future, professionally lead defined work packages Support the integration of sites, suppliers, and customers into the Catena-X ecosystem Prepare presentations, analyses, and project documentation Analyze processes, data requirements, and interfaces in the context of digitalization, sustainability, and quality management Ongoing studies in Industrial Engineering, Computer Science, Business Informatics, Business Administration, or a comparable field Interest in digitalization, data management, and the automotive industry Structured and independent working style with strong communication skills Proficient in MS Office applications (especially Excel and PowerPoint) Good German and English language skills Our offer: A mixed team of fresh talent and long-standing employees Extensive training and development opportunities A structured introduction program Are you interested? We are looking forward to receive your application. If you have any questions in the meantime do not hesitate to contact us. Please apply online in English and use our web portal at onemobility.recruitee.com. One Mobility GmbH Contact person: Anastasiia Masliuk, Global Recruiting Coordinator email: Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
    schema:employmentType "Student college, temporary" ;
